Suppose that 
\begin{align} 
 &\text{$A$~is a Cartan matrix of finite type;} 



\\ 
 &\text{$B_\circ=(b_{ij})$~is a sign-skew-symmetric matrix 
such that $A=A(B_\circ)$ and} 
\\ 
 &\text{$b_{ij} b_{ik} \geq 0$ for all $i,j,k$;} 
\\  &\text{$\mathbf{p}_\circ$~is  a 
$2n$-tuple of elements in $\mathbb{P}$ satisfying the normalization 
conditions.} 
\end{align} 
Then 
$\mathcal{A}(B_\circ,\mathbf{p}_\circ)$ is a 
cluster algebra of finite type.
